{title: 278 - Lord Jesus, Once You Spoke to Men}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #278 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 278}
{meta: category Holy Scriptures - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]Lord [F]Jesus, [Am]once You [Gm]spoke [F]to [Dm]men
[C]Upon [F]the [Am]mountain [C]and the [Am]plain,
[C]O [F]help us [Am]listen [Gm]now [F]as [Dm]then
[C]And wonder at Your [F/C]words again.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C]We [F]all have [Am]secret [Gm]fears [F]to [Dm]face,
[C]Our [F]minds and [Am]motives [C]to [Am]amend.
[C]We [F]seek Your [Am]truth, we [Gm]need [F]Your [Dm]grace,
[C]Our living Lord and [F/C]present [Gm]friend.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[C]The [F]gospel [Am]speaks; and [Gm]we [F]receive
[C]Your [F]light, Your [Am]love, [C]Your own command.
[C]O [F]help us [Am]live what [Gm]we [F]believe,
[C]In daily word of [F/C]heart and [Gm]hand.
{end_of_verse}
